          },
          "claim_2": {
            "type": "claim",
            "lang": "en",
            "text": "Lovelace was the only legitimate daughter of the poet Lord Byron and Anna Isabella Noel Byron. Byron separated from his wife a month after Ada was born and left England forever four months later. He commemorated their parting in a poem that begins: \"Is your face like your mother's, my beautiful daughter? ADA! Only daughter of my house and heart.\"",
